MLX v0.32.3's ~CudaHandle, backported to v0.32.2 (upstream: ml-explore/mlx v0.32.3,
mlx/backend/cuda/cuda_utils.h): the destructor no longer checks the destroy's
error, which aborted the process at exit when the CUDA driver was already
unloading ("Destroy(handle_) failed: driver shutting down"; fenrir, x86_64,
2026-10-20; genclj-kw88). Applied by native/build-mlx.sh cuda13-source.

--- a/mlx/backend/cuda/cuda_utils.h
+++ b/mlx/backend/cuda/cuda_utils.h
@@ -26,11 +26,10 @@
   }
 
   ~CudaHandle() {
-    // Skip if there was an error to avoid throwing in the destructors
-    if (cudaPeekAtLastError() != cudaSuccess) {
-      return;
+    // Skip error check to avoid throwing in destructors.
+    if (handle_ != nullptr) {
+      Destroy(handle_);
     }
-    reset();
   }
 
   CudaHandle(const CudaHandle&) = delete;
